  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Kafer Nabo SYR</p>\r\n<div>\u00a0</div>\r\n<div><a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1348/\">Inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2011 as part of the \"Ancient Villages of Northern Syria\" under criteria iii, iv, and v of UNESCO's World Heritage List <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://whc.unesco.org/en/criteria/\">Operational Guidelines</a>.</div>\r\n<div>\u00a0</div>\r\n<div>Specific archaeological components include:</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Ruins of an <strong>Byzantine church</strong> and numerous <strong>residential buildings</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient place, located in modern Syria, with remains of an ancient church and residential buildings. Inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2011 as part of the \"Ancient Villages of Northern Syria.\"",
